Following the initial missing value topological screening and signal correction, a stringent two-tier quality control module was implemented. This stage ensures that only robust, highly reproducible metabolic features with true biological origins are propagated to downstream statistical learning. A total of **{{ lq_pre_total }}** features (**{{ lq_pre.get('mar_count', 'N/A') }}** MAR and **{{ lq_pre.get('mnar_count', 'N/A') }}** MNAR) entered this stage.

**Tier 1: Background Noise Elimination (Blank/QC Ratio Check)**

To filter out ubiquitous environmental contaminants, solvent impurities, and instrument background noise, a Blank/QC intensity ratio check was applied. Features with an average Blank-to-QC ratio exceeding the threshold of {{ lq_thresh.get('blank_qc_ratio_tol', 'N/A') }} were discarded. This procedure pruned a total of **{{ lq_drop.get('dropped_by_blank', {}).get('total', 'N/A') }}** features. Post-Blank check, **{{ lq_post_blank_total }}** features survived.

**Tier 2: Analytical Reproducibility Check (QC RSD Check)**

Subsequently, to guarantee strict technical reproducibility, an RSD threshold of {{ lq_thresh.get('qc_rsd_tol', 'N/A') }} was applied to the pooled QC samples. Crucially, this step was executed exclusively on MAR features. MNAR features, which often represent genuine biological signals near the limit of detection (LOD), were exempted. Consequently, **{{ lq_drop.get('dropped_by_rsd', {}).get('total', 'N/A') }}** MAR features failed this reproducibility test.

Ultimately, the low-quality feature filtering cascade yielded a robust, high-confidence matrix containing **{{ lq_post_rsd_total }}** purified metabolic features (**{{ lq_post_rsd.get('mar_count', 'N/A') }}** MAR and **{{ lq_post_rsd.get('mnar_count', 'N/A') }}** MNAR).

