Systematic analytical variation, including global concentration differences, dilution effects, and residual instrument sensitivity shifts, was addressed before downstream statistical analysis.
{% if is_auto_norm %}
**Automatic Normalization Selection**

The normalization strategy was selected automatically from predefined log-only, sample-wise scaling, distribution-alignment, and variance-stabilizing candidates. Each candidate was evaluated on a common log-like view using four label-independent criteria: QC relative log expression (RLE) alignment change, QC variance stabilization, QC structure distance improvement, and sample structure preservation. The robust Log2-only strategy served as the neutral reference for candidate scoring, while the sample structure term combined actual-sample neighborhood trustworthiness, distance-rank preservation, and distance-scale preservation. The selected strategy was **{{ norm_selection.get('selected_label', norm_selection.get('selected_method', norm_method)) | replace('_', ' ') }}**
{%- if norm_selection.get('selected_score') is number %} with an overall score of **{{ norm_selection.get('selected_score') | round(3) }}**{%- endif -%}
{%- if norm_selection.get('selection_margin') is number %} and a score margin of **{{ norm_selection.get('selection_margin') | round(3) }}**{%- endif %}.

{%- elif norm_method == 'ROBUST_LOG_ONLY' %}
**Robust Log2 Transformation Only**

Sample-wise intensity correction was bypassed, and a robust Log2 transformation was applied to compress the dynamic range while preserving the original sample-wise scaling structure.

{%- elif norm_method == 'QUANTILE' %}
**Global Quantile Normalization**

A standalone global quantile normalization was applied. By imposing identical statistical distributions across all samples, it effectively mitigates complex, non-linear instrumental drifts.
{%- if is_log %} Prior to quantile alignment, a robust Log2 transformation was applied to stabilize variance.{%- endif %}

{%- elif norm_method == 'VSN' %}
**Variance Stabilizing Normalization (VSN)**

To address the heteroscedasticity inherent in mass spectrometry data, VSN was applied. The internal optimization engine determined the maximum likelihood parameters for the variance stabilization curve, converging on a structural scale factor of **{{ "%0.3e" | format(vsn_p.get('vsn_scale', 0)) if vsn_p.get('vsn_scale') is number else 'N/A' }}** and a generalized baseline shift of **{{ "%0.3e" | format(vsn_p.get('vsn_shift', 0)) if vsn_p.get('vsn_shift') is number else 'N/A' }}**. This transformation shifts the data into a generalized logarithmic space (glog) optimized for multivariate modeling.

{%- else %}
**Global Intensity Correction (Sample-wise)**

To mitigate analytical baseline fluctuations across the injection sequence, the data matrix underwent sample-wise normalization utilizing the **{{ norm_method }}** algorithm.
{%- if is_log %} Following sample calibration, a robust Log2 transformation was applied to stabilize variance.{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}

**Normalization Dashboard**
{% if is_auto_norm %}
The normalization dashboard summarizes the automatic method ranking through a weighted score-contribution panel and then visualizes the diagnostic evidence supporting the selected method.
{%- else %}
Because a fixed normalization method was specified, no candidate-ranking score panel was generated. The normalization dashboard instead reports the same QC and sample structure diagnostics for the applied method.
{% endif %}

Specifically, {% if is_auto_norm %}QC RLE alignment{% else %}QC relative log expression (RLE) alignment{% endif %} is evaluated using the median RLE center offset and RLE spread; QC variance stabilization is evaluated from the dependence between feature-wise mean QC log2 intensity and robust QC dispersion; QC structure distance improvement is assessed through distance-to-pooled-QC-centroid and QC-QC pairwise-distance changes; and sample structure preservation is monitored using actual-sample neighborhood trustworthiness together with distance-rank and distance-scale preservation diagnostics.

