## 2. Global Data Quality Assessment

{% set qa_base = raw_dataset.get('qa_assessments', {}) -%}
{%- set corr_method = qa_base.get('correlation', {}).get('method', 'spearman') %}

A fixed QA suite is run for each stage snapshot to show how processing changed the data. Its dashboards track QC or batch correlation, QC and biological-sample RSD distributions, PCA structure, and multivariate outliers, with optional internal-standard and outlier-reference-feature diagnostics. Candidate scores and stage-specific evidence remain in their respective processing results rather than the QA suite.

### 2.1 Feature Reproducibility

Pooled-QC and biological-sample RSDs were calculated separately. Pooled-QC RSD quantifies analytical precision, whereas RSD across biological samples is retained as a descriptive guardrail against unintended compression of sample heterogeneity; it is not an optimization target.

{% set rsd_guardrail = rsd_guardrail | default({}) -%}
{% if rsd_guardrail.get('available') -%}
The proportion of features with calculable pooled-QC RSD below 10% changed from **{{ rsd_guardrail.get('raw_qc_low_pct') | round(1) }}%** ({{ rsd_guardrail.get('raw_qc_low_count') }}/{{ rsd_guardrail.get('raw_qc_total') }}) in the raw matrix to **{{ rsd_guardrail.get('final_qc_low_pct') | round(1) }}%** ({{ rsd_guardrail.get('final_qc_low_count') }}/{{ rsd_guardrail.get('final_qc_total') }}) at the final **{{ rsd_guardrail.get('final_stage') }}** stage. In contrast, the proportion of retained features with RSD above 30% across biological samples changed from **{{ rsd_guardrail.get('raw_actual_high_pct') | round(1) }}%** ({{ rsd_guardrail.get('raw_actual_high_count') }}/{{ rsd_guardrail.get('raw_actual_total') }}) to **{{ rsd_guardrail.get('final_actual_high_pct') | round(1) }}%** ({{ rsd_guardrail.get('final_actual_high_count') }}/{{ rsd_guardrail.get('final_actual_total') }}). This broad distribution is interpreted together with sample-structure diagnostics and is consistent with retained between-sample heterogeneity after QC-oriented preprocessing.
